mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">课程简介（英文）</font></span></b><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">Course </font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">Description</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-spacerun:'yes';">&nbsp;</span></span></b><b><span
                                    style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">(</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">in English</font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">)</span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><div>The content of this course is developed around the core of "common tumors, supplemented by rare types, extended with cutting-edge advances, and supported by clinical practice", and is specifically divided into two major modules: theoretical teaching and clinical practice.</div>
<h3>(I) Theoretical Teaching</h3>
<div>It is structured according to the logic of "General Theory - Specific Topics - Interdisciplinary Fields", covering the entire spectrum of gynecological tumors, with explanations integrating the dual dimensions of "basic key points + research progress". The General Theory chapter introduces an overview of research advances in gynecological malignancies, sorting out the development context of the field, the evolution of core diagnosis and treatment technologies, as well as current research hotspots and challenges. The Specific Topics include a special section on cervical cancer, covering research progress, fertility-preserving treatment, rare malignant tumors, and diagnosis, treatment and prognosis management of recurrent cervical cancer. The special section on uterine tumors includes research progress and fertility-preserving treatment of endometrial cancer, pathological classification of uterine sarcomas, and key and difficult issues as well as advances in diagnosis and treatment. The special section on ovarian tumors covers epithelial ovarian malignancies, sex cord-stromal tumors, germ cell tumors, and treatment strategies for recurrent ovarian cancer. The special section on other gynecological tumors introduces vulvar and vaginal cancer, gestational trophoblastic neoplasms, and high-risk pregnancy-related gestational trophoblastic neoplasms. In addition, it involves interdisciplinary and cutting-edge fields of gynecological tumors, including gynecological tumor genetics, and content related to the malignant transformation of endometriosis and adenomyosis.</div>
<h3>(II) Clinical Practice</h3>
<div>Centered on the core form of "Multidisciplinary Team (MDT) collaboration", it helps students connect theory with clinical practice. By observing the diagnosis and treatment discussions of complex cases (such as advanced ovarian cancer and recurrent cervical cancer) by the gynecological oncology MDT team (including gynecology, pathology, radiology, oncology, etc.), students will learn the logic of case reporting, methods for integrating multidisciplinary opinions, and the process of clinical decision-making. After class, students can review theoretical knowledge in combination with demonstration cases to deepen their understanding.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>The course lasts for 16 teaching weeks, including 32 class hours of theoretical courses and 4 class hours of clinical internships.</div></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
